  "text": "Heart failure (HF) is a prevalent cardiovascular disease, influencing 1%−3% of the general adult demographic and showing an incremental trend in recent years. The heavy burden of HF leads to a high cost of medication and a poor prognosis. The mortality rate among these patients is relatively high, with one-year mortality ranging from 15%−30% [39], underscoring the critical need for an indicator that can predict subsequent adverse events effectively and simply. Based on the symptoms, HF could be classified as acute HF and chronic HF [1]"
